  "answer": "Based on the CDC and CBS News data:\n\n**Federal licenses in 2021 (CBS News):**\n- Wisconsin: 95,430\n- Ohio: 208,661\n- Michigan: 109,835\n- Missouri: 113,351\n\n**Homicide deaths in 2022 (CDC):**\n- Wisconsin: 266\n- Ohio: 744\n- Michigan: 538\n- Missouri: 555\n\n**Ratios (licenses ÷ homicides):**\n- Wisconsin: 95,430 / 266 = **358.76**\n- Ohio: 208,661 / 744 = **280.46**\n- Michigan: 109,835 / 538 = **204.15**\n- Missouri: 113,351 / 555 = **204.24**\n\n**Michigan has the lowest ratio** at approximately 204.15 federal licenses per homicide death.",
